---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../styles/articles.css';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---

<Layout title="Standards & Terminology — CABE" description="Publication references for CBOR, COSE, ACP 240, and NATO confidentiality labelling and metadata binding.">
  <main class="page" id="main" tabindex="-1">
    <header class="page__header">
      <div class="container">
        <span class="section-label">Reference</span>
        <h1 class="page__title">Standards &amp; Terminology</h1>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="page__body">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="article-prose reference-copy">
          <section aria-labelledby="ietf">
            <h2 id="ietf">IETF</h2>
            <div class="publication">
              <h3><a href="https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc8949">RFC 8949</a> — Concise Binary Object Representation (CBOR)</h3>
              <p class="publication-meta">Internet Engineering Task Force (IETF).</p>
              <p>Defines CBOR, including the deterministic encoding requirements used by <a href={`${base}/spec/arch/#serialization`}>CABE-ARCH to serialize Attribute Sets</a>.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="publication">
              <h3><a href="https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc9052">RFC 9052</a> — CBOR Object Signing and Encryption (COSE): Structures and Process</h3>
              <p class="publication-meta">Internet Engineering Task Force (IETF).</p>
              <p>Defines the <code>COSE_Encrypt0</code> and <code>COSE_Encrypt</code> structures used for CABE Envelopes by the <a href={`${base}/spec/cbes/#overview`}>CABE Baseline Envelope Structure (CBES)</a>.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="publication">
              <h3><a href="https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc9053">RFC 9053</a> — CBOR Object Signing and Encryption (COSE): Initial Algorithms</h3>
              <p class="publication-meta">Internet Engineering Task Force (IETF).</p>
              <p>Specifies COSE algorithms and parameters, including authenticated encryption and key wrapping. Cited in the <a href={`${base}/spec/cbes/#normative-references`}>CBES normative references</a>.</p>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section aria-labelledby="cceb">
            <h2 id="cceb">CCEB</h2>
            <div class="publication">
              <h3><a href="https://wss.apan.org/s/CCEB/public/Forms/acps.aspx">ACP 240(A)</a> — Data-Centric Interoperability Concepts and Design Requirements</h3>
              <p class="publication-meta">Combined Communications-Electronics Board (CCEB), 8 May 2025.</p>
              <p>Cited by <a href={`${base}/spec/acp240/`}>CABE-ACP240</a>, which maps selected classification and labelling concepts from ACP 240 and STANAG 4774 to CABE Attributes.</p>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section aria-labelledby="nato">
            <h2 id="nato">NATO</h2>
            <div class="publication-access">
              <p>Full NATO STANAGs are generally not publicly downloadable. NATO UNCLASSIFIED and NATO RESTRICTED documents are distributed through <a href="https://www.dsp.dla.mil/Specs-Standards/International-Standardization-Documents/">official channels</a>; public access depends on release authorisation. The entries below use public catalogue records and published reference material.</p>
              <p>To obtain full documents, contact your national NATO delegation or search the <a href="https://nso.nato.int/nso/nsdd/main/standards">NATO Standardization Office (NSO) standards database</a> by standard number, for example <code>4778</code> for STANAG 4778.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="publication">
              <h3><a href="https://nso.nato.int/nso/nsdd/main/standards/ap-details/1967/EN">ADatP-4774</a> — Confidentiality Metadata Label Syntax</h3>
              <p class="publication-meta">NATO Standardization Office. Edition A, Version 1, 20 December 2017; covered by STANAG 4774, Edition 1.</p>
              <p>Specifies confidentiality labels. <a href={`${base}/spec/acp240/#defined-attributes`}>CABE-ACP240</a> maps the policy identifier, classification, releasability, context and “ONLY” categories to the <code>p</code>, <code>s</code>, <code>r</code>, <code>c</code> and <code>o</code> Attributes.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="publication">
              <h3><a href="https://nso.nato.int/nso/nsdd/main/standards/ap-details/1968/EN">ADatP-4778</a> — Metadata Binding Mechanism</h3>
              <p class="publication-meta">NATO Standardization Office. Edition A, Version 1, 26 October 2018; covered by STANAG 4778, Edition 1.</p>
              <p>Defines a mechanism for binding metadata to data objects. CABE’s Attribute Set binding is specified in <a href={`${base}/spec/cbes/#header-fields`}>CBES</a>, which places the Attribute Set in a COSE protected header.</p>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section aria-labelledby="publication-terminology">
            <h2 id="publication-terminology">Publication terminology</h2>
            <p><strong>ACP</strong> means Allied Communications Publication. ACP 240 is issued by CCEB.</p>
            <p><strong>STANAG</strong> means <a href="https://www.nato.int/en/what-we-do/deterrence-and-defence/standardization">NATO Standardization Agreement</a>. It records nations’ agreement to implement a standard.</p>
            <p><strong>ADatP</strong> means Allied Data Processing Publication, a NATO publication series. ADatP-4774 and ADatP-4778 contain the technical specifications covered by their respective STANAGs.</p>
          </section>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>

<style>
  .reference-copy { max-width: 790px; }
  .publication-access { margin-bottom: 24px; }
  .publication + .publication { margin-top: 24px; }
  .publication p { margin-top: 8px; }
  .publication-meta { color: var(--quiet); font-size: 13px; }
</style>
